\par
     We will take her back to the surface, something whispered.\par
\par
     Alysha said, "Not before I speak with her."\par
\par
     As you will.\par
\par
     Alysha crouched in front of the young woman, touched her arms. "Ensign . . . Janny. Look at me, please."\par
\par
     Perralta lifted her tear-stained face. Alysha touched thumbs to the tracks and gently wiped the Asanii's cheeks. "Ssh," Alysha said. "The dream is over."\par
\par
     "I loved him," Perralta said. Her eyes were wounded, resigned. "It wasn't his fault. He got sick."\par
\par
     "I know," Alysha said. "Janny, I need you to do something for me."\par
\par
     The woman wiped at her nose. "Yes, sir, anything."\par
\par
     "I need you to go back and tell Commander Basil everything's okay. That she mustn't interrupt what's going on, but that we're all safe."\par
\par
     "Yes, sir," Perralta said, eyes downcast.\par
\par
     "Ensign," Alysha said. When Perralta didn't look up, Alysha bent so she could see into the girl's green eyes.\par
\par
     "Sir, I'm so sorry," Perralta said. "I messed up everything with a pathetic girl's dream. . . . "\par
\par
     "Janny, there's nothing pathetic about your nightmare," Alysha said. "You were young and a terrible thing happened to you. Why are you surprised that it still haunts you?"\par
\par
     "I thought I should just get over it," Perralta said. "It was so long ago. I thought I was weak."\par
\par
     "You thought to overcome something like that alone?" Alysha said, gentling her voice. "It's no shame to ask for help, Janny."\par
\par
     Perralta looked at her. "Have you?"\par
\par
     "Asked for help?" Alysha said. She smiled faintly and said, "It's how I met Laelkii. Collapsing on her doorstep. I still do that sometimes."\par
\par
     "You? You never collapse . . . "\par
\par
     "Everyone collapses, Janny."\par
\par
     She could see in the ensign's eyes that Perralta did not believe her. Alysha touched the woman's cheek. "Go to the Commander. The message is important."\par
\par
     "Yes, sir."\par
\par
     "And get counseling, please, Ensign," Alysha said. She tried for gentle humor and said, "There's a lot to be said for uninterrupted sleep."\par
\par
     Perralta smiled weakly. "Yes, sir."\par
\par
     Alysha stepped away and said, You may take her back now.\par
\par
     The golden lines curled around Perralta's body. As Alysha watched, the girl was reduced to coppery lines herself until she faded from view.\par
\par
     You are grieved, the waters said.\par
\par
     "Yes," Alysha said. She rechecked her braided line and headed back the way she'd come. Perhaps Darya and Felsha had had better luck with Steffis.\par
