     "You told us to talk to the First Commander, and we did that," Darya said. "We changed our minds about leaving."\par
\par
     "Just when the shuttle arrived, too," Felsha added.\par
\par
     "We thought someone should be here to greet you," Darya finished.\par
\par
     Alysha chuckled.\par
\par
     "We have food," Darya said.\par
\par
     Felsha added, "And clothing. Are we waiting again, sir?"\par
\par
     "Yes," Alysha said.\par
\par
     "Can we talk to the shore while we wait?" Darya asked.\par
\par
     "Yes," Alysha said again, then idly, "I could use the food and clothing. I feel bruised from the skin up." Which she became aware of as she said it: so long beneath the water, the currents constantly tugging at her pelage, and her skin did feel irritated.\par
\par
     "Towel!" Felsha squeaked and ran back toward the rock.\par
\par
     They brought her a towel and a full uniform and a small meal. She donned the abbreviated stretchsuit that went under the uniform but left the tunic, pants and boots folded together since she would not be leaving this island by eagle. The small meal she ate sparingly, and remembered not at all what it had encompassed once it was gone.\par
\par
     With her eyes on the waves and her people wandering the island behind her, Alysha waited.\par
\par
