     Taylitha drank, laced her fingers around the mug and stared out the window. Alysha could trace the lines that remained beneath the other woman's eyes from lack of sleep, but those would pass. Nothing in Taylitha's past had given her the fault lines that could prevent her from healing; that was one of her blessings. Hopefully the faults in Alysha's soul would mend, and she could shake off the faint unease that had resumed with the notion of touching other people, of having them know her.\par
\par
     "I guess you have to have a little of both," Taylitha said. "The ability to be close to something or someone, no matter the cost . . . the ability to hold things apart from you when they need to be held apart. But how do you know which is the right time?"\par
